# Accumulate every stdin line into a loop-carried mutable variable, then print
# the collected text once the source closes.
#
# The loop's induction extent is the source's own domain, so the read of `seen`
# compiles to a `StoreDenseRead` whose trigger iterates that source. That is a
# second read of the source, from the store rather than from the chain that
# reads the source's values.

seen := ""
for line in stdin():
    seen := seen + line + ";"
seen
